    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 14 tests pass, including the two new `Cp07Tests` (`coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`). The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both acceptable on input (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and present on output (`OwnerDto`). The `format: date` type generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name automatically in both directions, so no mapper changes were needed.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the incoming payload doesn't provide one (a supplied value is preserved).\n\n4. **Schema/seed SQL** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql), and added the corresponding `NULL` to the positional seed inserts in the hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` (h2/postgres already use explicit column lists). The tests run against hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required, not optional.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 14, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
